<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101699" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφιγκ-τήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which binds tight, lace, band</i>, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμας σφιγκτῆρα . . κεκρύφαλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.206
				</span></i>
			 (Antip. Sid.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. δεσμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					16.391
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>muscle closing an aperture</i> which naturally remains in the
			state of contraction, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.7
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.23.55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				4.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.78
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>a Tarentine</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιτών</span>, prob. because <i>laced
				tight to the body</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
